{
  "requirement": "The method is declared under {cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.running-criteria.check_inputs`.\n\nThe method resolves the recorded dependencies through graph operations and\nfingerprinting, comparing each with its saved observation. A fingerprint\nmismatch returns `Ok(false)` and permits an early return; it need not resolve\nlater dependencies. An encountered dependency-resolution failure returns an\nerror.\n\nThe method observes the current state that the caller intends to inspect.\nFreshness checking has a separate observation scope from criterion execution.\nChecked observations enter the new trace when execution explicitly reads\nor delivers them.\nA checked snapshot can be reused if it still represents the current state.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The tests cover each obligation in `requirements.sdk.graph.evidence.checking_records`. I did not read the implementation. Expected behavior comes from the requirement text, and the assertions enforce it.\n\n- **Resolve and compare each dependency; a mismatch returns `Ok(false)`.**\n  - `wildcard_versions_still_check_inputs_and_errors` covers a changed node fingerprint and a different fingerprint scheme.\n  - `a_matching_dependency_does_not_hide_a_later_changed_dependency` covers a later changed node dependency and a later changed `OutgoingEdges` dependency. A matching earlier dependency does not mask them.\n  - `labeled_selections_track_only_target_membership_without_reading_contents` covers edge selections. Unrelated-label changes stay current, target-set changes become stale, and no content reads happen.\n  - `changing_one_criteria_input_does_not_invalidate_another` and `absence_certification_is_invalidated_by_the_first_selected_root` cover `Validator::check_inputs` returning false for the changed record and true for the unchanged one.\n  - `input_checking_and_execution_keep_separate_observations` and `dependency_resolution_failures_do_not_execute_or_replace_saved_answers` also assert `Ok(false)` and `Ok(true)` through `check_inputs`.\n- **Early return is permitted.** Nothing requires it, so it needs no test.\n- **A dependency-resolution failure returns an error.**\n  - `dependency_resolution_failures_do_not_execute_or_replace_saved_answers` fails node reads and then edge listing. It asserts `check_inputs` returns `Err(\"read\")` or `Err(\"edges\")`. In the edge case the earlier node dependency resolves first. It also asserts the saved record is not replaced and nothing is executed.\n  - `wildcard_versions_still_check_inputs_and_errors` and `labeled_selections_track_only_target_membership_without_reading_contents` assert `is_current` returns `Err` for read and edge failures.\n- **Checking observes the current state the caller intends to inspect.** `requirement_edges_and_input_freshness_use_the_sdk` checks real SDK domain observations. A changed reference set makes the record stale, and a retained snapshot keeps its fingerprint.\n- **Checking has a separate observation scope from execution, and checked observations enter the new trace only through an explicit read or delivery.**\n  - `input_checking_and_execution_keep_separate_observations` and `historical_freshness_reads_do_not_enter_the_replacement_trace` assert this. The new record contains only the explicitly read dependency, and the read log shows the checked reads were not carried over.\n  - `refresh_evaluates_missing_incompatible_or_changed_evidence_with_a_fresh_trace` asserts a fresh trace for each cause: missing, revision, contents and successors.\n  - `typed_loading_reports_decode_errors_even_for_stale_evidence` asserts that loading performs no input reads.\n  - `source_reads_track_optional_dependencies_and_empty_searches_remain_discovery` covers delivery through tools, with and without a recorded dependency.\n- **A checked snapshot can be reused if it still represents the current state.** This is permissive wording. `requirement_edges_and_input_freshness_use_the_sdk` also checks that a retained snapshot's fingerprint is unaffected by later file changes.\n\nI found no unmarked relevant tests and no acknowledged gaps.",
